From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:55:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] combase: Ask the object for the interface before building a
 stub for it.

marshal_object() built the interface stub first and only then, through the stub's
connection and the new ifstub, found out whether the object had the interface at all.
IRemUnknown::RemQueryInterface marshals every interface asked for, so each remote query
for one an object lacks loaded the interface's proxy/stub factory, built a stub and
failed with an ERR: a PowerPoint session driven by a script logged 216 of them, nearly
all the script engine asking PowerPoint's objects for IDispatchEx.  E_NOINTERFACE is the
answer there, not an error; query first and return it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b8692b5ff885e19f9e08ae90eedc7e6af8d0df23)

diff --git a/dlls/combase/marshal.c b/dlls/combase/marshal.c
index 6e3d35ce580..2f0fbbaa714 100644
--- a/dlls/combase/marshal.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/marshal.c
@@ -889,10 +889,20 @@ HRESULT marshal_object(struct apartment *apt, STDOBJREF *stdobjref, REFIID riid,
     ifstub = stub_manager_find_ifstub(manager, riid, mshlflags);
     if (!ifstub) {
         IRpcStubBuffer *stub = NULL;
+        IUnknown *iface;
+
+        /* An object without the interface has nothing to marshal.  Asked from
+         * another apartment, by IRemUnknown::RemQueryInterface, that is the
+         * answer rather than an error, and it takes no stub to find out. */
+        hr = IUnknown_QueryInterface(manager->object, riid, (void **)&iface);
+        if (hr == S_OK)
+            IUnknown_Release(iface);
+        else
+            TRACE("Object %p has no %s, hr %#lx.\n", manager->object, debugstr_guid(riid), hr);
 
         /* IUnknown doesn't require a stub buffer, because it never goes out on
          * the wire */
-        if (!IsEqualIID(riid, &IID_IUnknown))
+        if (hr == S_OK && !IsEqualIID(riid, &IID_IUnknown))
         {
             IPSFactoryBuffer *psfb;
 
